  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the acceleration of monkey while moving down.</p><p>F.B.D of monkey while moving downward</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/19e2e280-cfda-422b-ba66-07f93b617282-image.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 183px;\" /></p><p>Using Newton&#39;s second law of motion,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p></blockquote><blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the acceleration of monkey while moving up.</p><p>F.B.D of monkey while moving up</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/348ae634-3957-4545-aa46-5e68fb90634d-image.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 186px;\" /></p><p>Using Newton&#39;s second law of motion</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>750</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>Breaking strength of rope&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>750</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo></math> Rope will break while monkey is moving upward.</p></blockquote>",
